  "details": "Recently I’ve got an idea, how to fix the major problem of VRChat, about the ages of the players, and about the not safe for work content.\n\nSo, the main idea is that, when you’re uploading an avatar/world, you need to do a age restriction. The content maker chooses themself, what age this or that content suppose to be. For example: Someone created an avatar that is likely more for 18+ people. And people who are less than 18+, cannot see this avatar. The same thing about the worlds. If the creator of this world made it for 18+, people who are underage, will have no access to this world.\n\nOr for example add an option, where you can choose YOURSELF what content you're fine to see. NSFW, VIOLENCE, and more. Just like the feature to block automatically avatars that are very poor.",
